{
  "about": "Every figure with a unit (%, points, euros, PPS) typed into the interface strings or the content pages, pair by pair, with its kind (src/lib/quoted-figures.mjs, KINDS: illustrative, rule, past, finding). Typed figures do not follow the data, so the site check (scripts/checks.mjs, section 11) fails on a pair whose figures are not listed here exactly, and on an entry that no longer matches any text: writing or changing a figure means looking at it, and the list only shrinks. A figure about the latest month has no kind: show it in a chart, not in a sentence. Add or change an entry only with a maintainer agreeing. npm run figures:report shows each pair with its figures and text. A past entry also says, figure by figure (its English figures, in order), where each comes from under checks: a series the build exports, which the release step check-figures recomputes from the data (src/traceconomics/quoted_figures.py), or the archived datasets it rests on (sources, with a reason), whose change holds an automatic release for a person to read the sentence again.",
